# Secret files — hard ban

The operator keeps live API keys and secrets in local files. Treat them as out of bounds forever.

## Never do any of the following

- Read, open, cat, type, Get-Content, or otherwise inspect `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.*.local`, or any file matching `.env.*` except `.env.example`
- Edit, write, patch, or delete those files (including "fix typos", "add a key", or "sync from example")
- Print, log, quote, or summarize values that might have come from them
- Ask the user to paste their API key into chat
- Commit `.env` or session files under `data/`

## Allowed instead

- Read and edit `.env.example` only (placeholders, no real secrets)
- Tell the user which *variable names* to set and where (e.g. `API_KEY`, `CHATBOT_URL`)
- Point scripts at `dotenv` / `process.env` without opening `.env`

If a task seems to require opening `.env`, stop and ask the user to change it themselves.
